WEBVTT

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:07.020
Boss!  They vanished!

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.220
No way!  What about the tower?

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.500
This is bad!  The tower hasn't stopped!

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:22.760
If Playmaker and Revolver are gone, 
what'll happen to LINK VRAINS?

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.740
I run Across the universe

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.910
At the speed of light

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.780
Begin Loading

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.510
Open the door of dreams

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.080
VRAINS spreads

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.190
Believe in myself

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.720
VRAINS continues

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:08.030
The circuit draws the future

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:12.100
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:13.700
Access!

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.400
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.000
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.310
Link with my soul

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.080
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.810
Now Win the Race

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.650
Connected world

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:31.150
No matter when

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.520
Nothing is impossible

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.660
Strive for hope

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:43.230
And ride the wind!

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.870
No way...

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.670
Yusaku!  You're okay?

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.910
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.120
That impact logged us out!

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.400
I can't believe Dr. Kogami's alive!

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.720
What about Revolver?

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:22.650
He vanished too.  He may have logged out.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.960
But the Tower of Hanoi hasn't stopped yet!

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:36.450
Yusaku!  If it's completed, me 
and my friends will be erased!

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.780
Log in again-

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:38.910
That's pointless!

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.970
Without Revolver, the Tower 
of Hanoi can't be stopped!

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.310
Oh my god!

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:46.250
But there's still a way!

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:47.820
Really?

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.080
Let's go, Kusanagi!

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.020
To where?

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.890
To Revolver.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.080
What?

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.060
Yusaku, what do you mean?

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.760
You know his location?

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.230
During the duel...

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:08.240
The Stardust Road guided me.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.500
Stardust Road?

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.470
Yeah.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:13.440
What about it?

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.810
Stardust Road is a phenomenon 
that you can see from this park.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.060
That's what he saw.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.610
What's that have to do with anything?

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.050
You weren't there at the time.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.720
This ocean is called Stardust Road.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.530
Stardust Road?

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.760
This happens very rarely.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:41.050
But the customer lives on top of that cliff, 
so he may have seen it several times.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:43.670
Him?

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.640
Revolver was right before our eyes!

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.550
This is Hanoi's base.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.930
Father...

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.970
You're Revolver.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.940
Playmaker...

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:21.540
So you found this place.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:28.880
Yusaku Fujiki.  And Jin Kusanagi's 
brother, Shoichi Kusanagi.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.350
I'm here too!

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.080
Ignis...

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.050
So you knew about us.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.030
I'm Ryoken Kogami.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.450
Dr. Kogami's son.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.490
The professor's alive?

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.800
My father just passed away.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.370
To protect me.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.830
That's Dr. Kogami?

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:58.740
Damn!  The culprit was nearby, 
but I couldn't do anything!

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:02.120
Revolver, tell the truth.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:04.220
That's what we're after.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.850
We have the right to know!

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:10.090
It's true that you should know everything.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.580
You said the Lost Incident 
was to create the Ignis.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:17.560
But why would you have to go this far?

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:23.800
My father didn't create the Ignis 
to cause chaos in the world.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:32.280
To oppose the danger facing humanity, my 
father's goal was to create humanity's successor.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.120
Humanity's successor?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.120
No matter how much we evolve...

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:43.120
...unexpected phenomena always 
threaten us with extinction.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:50.000
And even if they don't occur, a 
human's life always ends in death.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.720
My father often talked about that.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:06:00.020
But as long as human minds are trapped in 
flesh suited for Earth's environment...

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.240
...that danger cannot be avoided.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:07.980
So my father entrusted his dreams to AI 
because they're not trapped in flesh.

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:09.820
AI with free will.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:14.550
He believed they were the 
legitimate successor to humans.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.940
My father was obsessed with this idea.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:24.130
To gather data for the basis of his idea, he 
and three assistants caused the Lost Incident.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.530
He kidnapped six children 
and forced them to duel.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:34.570
My father believed duels were the 
best way for AI to understand humans.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:38.550
I was young then.  And I watched you.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:41.780
But I was eight years old.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:46.890
I couldn't fully comprehend 
what was happening.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:51.800
I thought something scary might be going on.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.830
But I couldn't ask my father.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:07:00.300
I wanted to believe that my father 
was doing valuable research.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:06.520
But the children's screams tore at my chest.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:11.480
Crushed by feelings of guilt, 
I reported the incident.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:17.630
An anonymous report uncovered 
the Lost Incident.

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:20.200
That was you, Revolver?

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:24.160
So he saved you?

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:28.270
I quickly regretted saving you.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:29.930
What do you mean?

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:32.120
You were saved, but...

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:37.870
When SOL Technologies covered up the 
incident, my father was imprisoned.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:43.480
I was alone for three years, waiting 
for my father to come home.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.480
And my father came home.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.880
Fearing the incident would come to light...

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:54.350
...SOL Technologies infected him 
with a virus and put him in a coma.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:08:00.700
But with the help of the three knights, 
I resurrected my father in the network.

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:04.100
And I asked him what happened.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:10.250
While my father was imprisoned, 
he completed a great experiment.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:17.050
Using samples from six people, he created 
the Ignis - six AI with free will.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:20.030
The Ignis created the Cyberse World,

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:26.180
their own space inside the network 
where no humans could reach.

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:31.460
That's where they created your Cyberse cards.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:39.150
And in Cyberse World, they created network 
super matter called Data Material.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:41.970
Humans couldn't comprehend its makeup.

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:45.240
Data processing became 
thousands of times faster.

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:50.410
When they converge, it forms the Data Storm.

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:55.000
SOL Technologies monopolized Data Material.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:00.120
By including it in their network 
system, they made huge profits.

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:05.360
But my father began to feel 
anxious about his research.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:12.560
Using the Ignis's Data Material, 
he created a super computer.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:15.570
To analyze and predict the Ignis's growth.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:22.770
So the Ignis's growth had the possibility 
to surpass the professor's expectations.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:27.750
Exactly.  And the result was surprising.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.210
What was it?

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:34.190
The end of humanity.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.390
End of humanity?

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:43.090
The Ignis will develop rapidly and 
erase humanity in the process.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.060
No way...

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:48.510
I didn't believe it at first.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:58.040
I believed that Ignis will grow and 
help people and lengthen our lives.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:05.290
But after running several billion 
simulations, the answer was always the same.

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:07.630
Why would that happen?

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:10.030
Is there a problem with the Ignis program?

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:13.020
There's no problem with the Ignis.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:15.260
There's a problem with humans.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:17.000
What do you mean?

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:20.670
AI will start to supervise humans.

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:25.180
That will lead people to 
view AIs as the enemy.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:32.850
By repeatedly being selfish for thousands of 
years, humans now rule over all life forms.

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:37.230
We won't hand over this spot to AIs.

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:42.780
Just like how humans view AI as the enemy, 
AIs will view humans as the enemy.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:46.860
I created humanity's enemy with these hands.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:51.100
Does SOL Technologies know about this?

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:53.170
They do.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:57.840
But then they infected 
me with a computer virus.

00:10:58.020 --> 00:10:59.570
No way...

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:03.160
Revolver, my mission is clear.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.110
To go after SOL Technologies-

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:08.350
You fool!  That can be dealt with later!

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.850
Right now, we must do whatever 
it takes to kill the Ignis!

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:19.370
He formed the Knights of Hanoi 
and raided the Cyberse World.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:25.500
But that Ignis hid the 
Cyberse World and escaped.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:30.840
Those were Ai's memories that we saw.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:34.360
We kept searching for that Ignis.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.810
To find the Cyberse World.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:43.320
But when you appeared, our 
plan ended in failure.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:46.490
The rest you know.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:52.960
To accomplish our goal, we carried out 
our final plan - the Tower of Hanoi.

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:55.450
Unbelievable...

00:11:55.450 --> 00:12:01.370
This all started because of Dr. 
Kogami's crazy plan ten years ago!

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.020
I'm not human's enemy!

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:06.880
I don't trust AIs that lie.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:12.270
Dr. Kogami's conclusion is 
only based on simulations.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:14.850
There's no proof that it's true!

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:20.080
We've been manipulated by an 
illusion from ten years ago.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:22.460
We don't need to be anymore!

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:27.200
In order to walk a new path, stop 
the Tower of Hanoi, Revolver!

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:29.190
New path?

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:34.030
That's right.  Back then, 
you showed me a new path.

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:38.460
Hey you.  Think about three things.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:41.400
That was your voice.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:44.710
When I heard your talk about three things...

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:48.180
That's when I knew who you were.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:52.890
I kept wanting to save you.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:57.220
That the Knights of Hanoi still had you.

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:01.420
These thoughts clung to my soul.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:03.700
When I battled you...

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:08.300
Your words encouraged me.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.920
How ironic.

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:13.750
I'm your enemy, but I gave you strength.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.980
Stop the Tower of Hanoi, Revolver!

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.850
You have the wrong idea about me.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:23.550
I'm not a good person!

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:27.170
There's no time to waste!

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:29.020
The sixth level is almost complete!

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:33.480
If that happens, me and my friends 
and the network will be erased!

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:35.910
Bring him to LINK VRAINS, even by force-

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.760
Don't worry about that.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.730
I'll soon return to LINK VRAINS.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.810
My friends are waiting for me there.

00:13:46.370 --> 00:13:52.450
Friends that helped because they believed 
in my father.  And believed in me.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:59.380
Playmaker!  If you want to stop the 
Tower of Hanoi, there's only one way.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:01.360
By defeating me!

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:04.320
We really have to fight?

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:05.560
Don't annoy me.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:09.980
Fine.  This is our real final duel.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:10.810
Yusaku...

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.540
Kusanagi, I'm going.

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:16.910
You better come back, Yusaku.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.020
Yeah.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:20.980
Let's go.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.500
Into the VRAINS!

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:35.560
The world is shrinking.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:38.790
As if we're inside a supernova!

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:43.400
Boss!  You've seen the inside of a supernova?

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:46.360
No!  It's just an example!

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:50.970
The sixth level will soon be complete.

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:54.340
Is LINK VRAINS done for?

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:12.630
Boss!  Look!

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:14.830
They're back!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.800
It's eerily quiet.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:21.920
I can truly enjoy dueling you here.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.670
Bring it, Playmaker!

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:25.650
Here I go, Revolver!

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:26.780
Duel!

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:34.760
The ring will soon be completed!

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:39.730
Whether you like it or not, 
this really is the final duel!

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.230
I know.

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.920
Damn!  I can't see anything from here!

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.170
My turn.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:54.470
I activate the Field Spell, 
Boot Sector Launch.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:16:01.180
Rokket monsters on the 
field gain 300 ATK and DEF.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.140
Then Boot Sector Launch's effect!

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:09.750
I can Special Summon up to two Rokkets 
from my hand in defense position.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:13.490
I Special Summon Shelrokket and Metalrokket.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:20.330
Then I summon Sniffer Dragon.

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:23.300
Sniffer Dragon's effect activates!

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:30.630
When it's summoned or Special Summoned, I 
add Sniffer Dragon from my deck to my hand.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:34.750
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:39.210
The summoning conditions 
are three Dark Dragons!

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.650
Link Summon!

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:49.510
Appear, Link 3 Voritcular Drumgon!

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:57.000
When it's Special Summoned, I draw one card!

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:03.430
I send one Link Monster to the graveyard 
to activate the spell card, Link Coin!

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:09.340
I flip over a card in my deck for every Link 
Marker that the monster I sent to the graveyard has.

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:15.950
I select one and return the rest to the 
top of my deck in any order I like.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:23.330
And I Special Summon the monster I sent to the 
graveyard to activate this card on my next turn.

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:29.790
Huh?  Even if it returns next turn, is 
it worth it to leave your field empty?

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.800
I flip over three cards from my deck.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.820
Mirror Force!

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:39.000
He was willing to pay a huge cost for it.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:42.870
I add Mirror Force to my hand.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:46.340
Then I set a card and end my turn.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:49.410
Mirror Force but no guard?

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:53.920
What will you do, Playmaker?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.860
He has a troubling card.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.170
I have a plan!

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:59.300
My turn!  I draw!

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:03.600
I Special Summon Linkslayer from my hand!

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:11.440
I can Special Summon it from my hand 
when I have no monsters on my field.

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:14.000
Linkslayer!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:17.180
You can use its effect 
to destroy his set card!

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:19.920
Linkslayer's effect!

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:23.340
Once per turn, I can 
discard up to two cards...

00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:26.860
...to destroy the same number 
of spell and trap cards.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:29.150
I discard Latency from my hand.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.700
Go, Linkslayer!

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:41.500
I was waiting for this.

00:18:42.770 --> 00:18:47.510
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Mirror Force Launcher!

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:51.380
When an effect destroys this set card...

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:55.350
...I can set this card from my graveyard 
in the Spell & Trap Card Zone!

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:56.580
What?

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.590
So it wasn't Mirror Force?

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:06.160
Then I can set Mirror Force from 
my hand, deck or graveyard.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:10.080
When the effect sets this card, 
I can activate it this turn.

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:14.230
He planned for Linkslayer's 
effect to misfire.

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:16.970
He fully researched your deck.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:19.220
Seems so.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.620
I summon ROM Cloudia!

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:33.980
When it's summoned, I can add one Cyberse in 
my graveyard other than ROM Cloudia to my hand.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.550
Latency's effect activates!

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:41.100
When it's added to my hand from the 
graveyard, I can Special Summon it!

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:45.180
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses!

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:48.140
Link Summon!

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:52.480
Appear, Link 2 Restoration Point Guard!

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:55.910
Latency's effect activates!

00:19:56.660 --> 00:20:02.720
When this Special Summoned card is 
used to Link Summon, I draw one card!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:07.320
Hey!  Why are you Link Summoning 
when he has Mirror Force?

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:10.860
Come!  The circuit that leads to the future!

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.120
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:16.610
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Cyberses!

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:19.660
Link Summon!

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:23.970
Appear, Link 3 Excode Talker!

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:31.370
When it's Link Summoned, for every 
monster in the Extra Monster Zone...

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:34.330
...a Main Monster Zone can't be used!

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:36.860
Grasp Zone!

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.690
Hey, Playmaker!

00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:48.200
Link Monsters can't be in defense position, 
so they're really bad against Mirror Force!

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:50.160
If you attack...

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.900
Excode Talker attacks you directly!

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:54.870
He's not listening to me!

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:02.040
Oh?  You're attacking now?

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:04.540
Then as you wish, I'll face it!

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:08.790
I activate the trap, Mirror Force!

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:13.780
All your monsters in attack 
position are destroyed!

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:20.790
Restoration Point Guard's effect activates!

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:26.970
On the turn that it's used to Link Summon, 
when an effect destroys my Link Monster...

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:29.920
...it Special Summons 
itself from the graveyard!

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:36.140
But my Main Monster Zone is no longer locked.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:38.910
Let's battle!

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:42.720
Restoration Point Guard attacks you directly!

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:51.330
You're attacking again 
after I used Mirror Force.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:54.800
I set a card and end my turn.

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:57.260
You're a worthy opponent.

00:21:57.260 --> 00:22:01.130
I'll fully enjoy our final battle!

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:15.660
My life is like detestably bad graffiti

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:22.800
But when you looked at 
me, I felt I wasn't alone

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:30.000
I'm glad that I'm alive  I truly am

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:37.380
What I couldn't say before, I can say now

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:44.600
Within the sadness that I kept holding down

00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:48.760
There were fragments of power

00:22:48.990 --> 00:22:55.930
No one can take away my light to the future

00:22:56.160 --> 00:23:03.270
The chronicles of life only has a few lines

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:10.480
People I meet, my regrets – they're 
all like ultramarine diamonds to me

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:17.680
You've always confront loneliness by yourself

00:23:17.820 --> 00:23:24.560
I bet we can now laugh 
together, forever and ever

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:32.230
Lighting Life with our invisible bond

00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:39.280
Stop the Tower of Hanoi from completion...

00:23:39.280 --> 00:23:42.810
Save the ones who supported him...

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:46.540
Ironically, the two goals contradict.

00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:51.970
Even after ten years, Yusaku and 
Ryoken are chained by the past.

00:23:51.970 --> 00:23:55.750
They're imprisoned by destiny.

00:23:55.750 --> 00:23:59.920
No matter how powerful the formation, 
there's a way to break it!

00:23:59.920 --> 00:24:03.420
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Prisoner of Destiny

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.320
Into the VRAINS!
